# Vite
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# The packed extension. `vscode/dist/extension.js` is committed and is what a
# .vsix carries; the archive around it is built on demand at install time and
# carries the version in its name, so a committed one is stale the moment the
# manifest moves.
vscode/*.vsix

# Claude worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# Scratch: nothing new here enters git. The drivers and issue notes already
# committed stay tracked — closed tickets cite those paths — because an ignore
# rule has no say over a file git is already following. Anything added from
# here on needs `git add -f` to make the case for itself.
.scratch/
